NickelOS: on a driver without implicit synchronization (NVIDIA), do not flip
a client's buffer that came without DRI3 1.4 sync points: nothing would tell
the compositor when the client's rendering into it is done. Copy it instead,
which glamor fences with Xwayland's own sync point (explicit sync) or waits
for (glFinish). Upstream allows the flip as soon as explicit sync is
available and then attaches the buffer with no sync at all.

--- a/hw/xwayland/xwayland-present.c
+++ b/hw/xwayland/xwayland-present.c
@@ -874,6 +874,16 @@
     if (!xwl_window || !xwl_window->allow_commits)
         return FALSE;
 
+#if defined(XWL_HAS_GLAMOR) && defined(DRI3)
+    /* Without implicit sync, a buffer that comes without sync points has
+     * nothing that says when the client's rendering into it is done; let
+     * the copy path (fenced by glamor) present it.
+     */
+    if (!xwl_glamor_supports_implicit_sync(xwl_window->xwl_screen) &&
+        !(vblank->acquire_syncobj && vblank->release_syncobj))
+        return FALSE;
+#endif /* defined(XWL_HAS_GLAMOR) && defined(DRI3) */
+
     buffer = xwl_pixmap_get_wl_buffer(pixmap);
     if (!buffer) {
         ErrorF("present: Error getting buffer\n");
